   "issues": [
     {"issue": "\"Their affiliated chapter 11 debtors and debtors in possession\" defines the released and bound \"Debtors\" only by reference to a footnote list that includes at least one non-U.S. entity (Aeropostale Canada Corp.), leaving the membership of the defined term arguable. The reach of every release and covenant turns on that boundary.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.07}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.07},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.08}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": "The defined term is opened but never closed (\"the “Bankruptcy Court)\"), a punctuation slip. It does not change the meaning, since the court is fully identified by name and case number.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.06},
     {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.05}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005",
   "issues": [
     {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.12},
     {"issue": "The delivery obligation is measured by the Detailed Delivery Schedule attached as Exhibit A, but Section 7 requires the Debtors to file a \"revised version of Exhibit A\" on May 20, 2016, leaving it open which schedule fixes the delivery dates. Nothing states that the revised exhibit becomes the operative Detailed Delivery Schedule.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.25}
   ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006",
